<article class="env-remark" id="03R2">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03R2">Remark <span data-tag="03R2">4.9.2.6</span>.</a> Let $\kappa $ be an ordinal. The following conditions are equivalent: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(1)$</dt>
<dd><p>
The ordinal $\kappa $ is a cardinal. That is, there exists a set $S$ such that $\kappa = |S|$. 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(2)$</dt>
<dd><p>
For every well-ordered set $(S, \leq )$ of order type $\kappa $, we have $\kappa = |S|$. 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(3)$</dt>
<dd><p>
The set of ordinals $\mathrm{Ord}_{&lt; \kappa }$ has cardinality $\kappa $. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
<p> See Corollary <a data-tag="03QH" href="/tag/03QH">4.9.1.23</a>. </p>
</article>
